<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. van Gogh is a 36-year-old painter with a first episode of psychosis five months ago, on aripiprazole 10 mg daily, and an alcohol use disorder on naltrexone, who comes for his yearly preventive visit eight weeks after his three-month review. He has had no voices, confusion, or suspiciousness since the six-week visit. He sleeps about seven hours and is painting most days, outdoors in the fields when the weather is good. He drinks one or two glasses of wine with dinner on some days and no spirits. He meets his therapist from the coordinated specialty care team every two weeks and the peer specialist monthly. He smokes his pipe each day. His mood is good and his PHQ-9 today is 4. He has no new concerns. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 36</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosis</td><td>No symptoms for more than three months on aripiprazole 10 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>One or two glasses of wine on some days; AUDIT-C 3</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 4; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Aripiprazole 10 mg daily; naltrexone 50 mg daily; thiamine 100 mg daily</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on a tablet in the waiting room and reviewed with him by Dr. Verhoeven. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and much better than in the winter</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Supported by a friend nearby and the coordinated specialty care team; selling some work again</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>AUDIT-C 3; no spirits since the spring; no drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Smokes a pipe daily</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks several kilometres most days to paint outdoors</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Eats two regular meals a day now, with fewer meals of only bread and coffee</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours on most nights, at regular times</td></tr><tr><td>Sun and heat</td><td>Paints in full sun for hours; rarely wears a hat or sunscreen</td></tr><tr><td>Work safety</td><td>Uses oil paints and solvents in his studio; cleans brushes with turpentine, with the window open</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Not in a relationship; uses condoms with new partners</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe; no firearm in the home</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

