    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Pneumococcal and hepatitis B vaccination started today; sun protection and studio ventilation advised. [S]<list><item>Hat and sunscreen when painting outdoors; paint in the shade at midday.</item><item>Clean brushes in a well-ventilated space and keep solvents capped.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">First episode of psychosis, provisional diagnosis, in remission on aripiprazole (F29)</content>. No psychotic symptoms for more than three months. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline are in his phone, and he has no firearm. He chose to write a psychiatric advance directive today. [S]<list><item>Continue aripiprazole 10 mg daily.</item><item>Six-month review in five weeks with the AIMS.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder on naltrexone (F10.20)</content>. Drinking much reduced; AUDIT-C 3. [S]<list><item>Continue naltrexone and thiamine; PEth and liver tests at six months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>120/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 4, from 13 at intake; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 3, from 9 at intake; in treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco cessation</td><td>Declined</td><td>Smokes a pipe daily; counseling and nicotine replacement offered; he is not ready and will say when he is</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Nonreactive in the first-episode workup at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Hepatitis C antibody drawn today; once for adults 18 to 79</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Not overweight, so screening is not due by age; fasting glucose 94 mg/dL and A1c 5.4% at the 12-week antipsychotic check; next yearly on aripiprazole</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at the 12-week antipsychotic check; yearly on aripiprazole; statin assessment begins at 40</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 45</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20, recommended for adults with alcohol use disorder</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No record of vaccination; dose 1 of 2 today, dose 2 at the six-month visit</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap given in the emergency department with the ear wound care</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>In the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Due</td><td>No dental visit for more than a year; advised to book one</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month review in five weeks with the AIMS, PEth, liver tests, blood count, and the second hepatitis B dose. Hepatitis C result by phone. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1889-07-20: six-month review: diagnosis, relapse prevention, movement check, and alcohol. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
